{"number":1,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Sort the faceted tree alphabetically (case-insensitive, by DISPLAY LABEL) at all three levels (operator 010/Q1). In `Facets.buildTree` (`Facets.fs:230-254`) change the branch sort from the structural `List.sortBy (fun b -> b.value)` (`:248`) to a case-insensitive sort by the branch display `label` (e.g. `List.sortWith` comparing with `System.String.Compare(a.label, b.label, System.StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)`). In BOTH host tree assemblies sort the top-level facet-group nodes and every entry-leaf child alphabetically by label, overriding the representation/corpus order: `MaterialsWindowView.fs:719-760` (the `entriesNode` children built from `filtered` and the `facetNodes` from `engineTree.facets`) and `LibraryWindowView.fs:844-898` (same shape plus the numeric-bucket branch projection). No other behaviour changes. Cover the branch-label sort in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` and the window-projection ordering in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`.","acceptance":"After buildTree runs over a fixed corpus, its branches MUST be ordered case-insensitively by display label, and both windows' projected trees MUST list facet groups and entry leaves alphabetically by label - unit- and headless-verified.","section":"Part A - Faceted tree: sorting, collapse, selection"}
{"number":2,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[1],"how_to":"Make the tree collapsible with persisted, collapsed-by-default expansion (operator). In `OpticalConstructor.Controls/FacetedTreeControls.fs`: add `toggleNode : string -> unit` to the `Handlers` record (`:149-167`) beside `selectNode`; in `nodeRows` (`:351-368`) render a per-parent disclosure chevron (a leaf with empty `children` shows none) whose pointer-press dispatches `handlers.toggleNode node.code` while the row label keeps dispatching `selectNode`, each keyed with `View.withKey` and carrying a stable `UiIds.FacetedTree` AutomationId added in `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`. In BOTH windows (`MaterialsWindowView.fs`, `LibraryWindowView.fs`) hold expansion in the Model as an elevated named type wrapping the expanded-code set (e.g. `type ExpandedNodes = ExpandedNodes of Set<string>` with `.value` and toggle members - never a naked `Set<string>` on the record surface), add a `Msg` + `update` arm that flips a code, and project each `TreeNode.expansion` as `ExpandedNode` only when its code is in the set and `CollapsedNode` otherwise - replacing every hardcoded `ExpandedNode` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:719-760`, `LibraryWindowView.fs:844-898`). Update the headless tests that assumed entry-leaves-first-and-expanded.","acceptance":"After a top-level node's chevron is clicked, the window Model MUST record it expanded and re-project its children (and collapse on a second click), and every top-level node MUST render `CollapsedNode` on first open - headless-verified in both windows."}
{"number":3,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"Make the selected tree node visibly distinct (operator). Add a `selectedCode : string` field to `FacetedTreeControls.State` (`:113-132`; empty string = none, matching the module's `activeRepresentation` convention `:124`,`:140`) and initialise it in `empty` (`:134-144`). In `nodeRows` (`:351-368`) paint the row whose `code` equals `state.selectedCode` with the existing `chosenBackground` (`:173`) instead of `idleBackground` (`:355`), plus a non-hue cue (thicker `borderThickness` or a leading marker glyph) so it reads colourblind-safe. Both hosts (`MaterialsWindowView.fs`, `LibraryWindowView.fs`) set `selectedCode` from the Model's already-tracked selected node code when projecting `State`. No handler signature changes - `selectNode` already exists (`:162`).","acceptance":"After a node is selected, exactly that row MUST render with `chosenBackground` plus its non-hue cue while every other row stays idle - headless-verified in both windows."}
{"number":4,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Re-seed the three coded-preset materials so their single-valued class is data (Part B mechanism; operator 010/Q2). In `MaterialLibrary.fs builtInEntries` (`:368-466`) change Silicon (`:371-377`), Langasite (`:378-385`), and the Vacuum spacer (`:434-441`) from `complexity = None` to `complexity = Some <valueTree>` with `properties = <valueTree>.toProperties`, following the existing seed convention every other built-in already uses (`:391-464`). The value trees encode: Silicon = Isotropic, dispersive, absorbing (mirror `euvSiliconComplexity` `:456`); Langasite = Uniaxial retaining its optical-activity component (mirror `uniaxialCrystalComplexity` `:424` plus `activeCrystalComplexity` `:464`); Vacuum = Isotropic, Transparent, constant (n = 1). Reproduce each preset's published physics through the existing dispersion-model ladder - do NOT add any classifier that evaluates the engine eps tensor. Unit tests in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` assert every entry in `builtInEntries` now carries `complexity = Some`, and that `LibraryFacets.anisotropyOf` returns Isotropic for Silicon, Uniaxial for Langasite, and Isotropic for Vacuum.","acceptance":"After the re-seed, every material in `builtInEntries` MUST carry `complexity = Some`, and `anisotropyOf` MUST classify Silicon Isotropic, Langasite Uniaxial, and the Vacuum spacer Isotropic - unit-verified with no engine-tensor evaluation.","section":"Part B - Facet totality via seeds"}
{"number":5,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[4],"how_to":"Make the Anisotropy and Transparency material facets total (operator 010/Q2). In `LibraryFacets.fs`: drop the `appliesTo` gate on `materialAnisotropyDef` (`:217-232`) so it is `fun _ -> ApplicableAttribute` and its `extract` reads `anisotropyOf complexity` for every entry (all carry `complexity` after step 4; a defensive `None` yields `[]`). Drop the `appliesTo` gate on `materialTransparencyDef` (`:252-267`) so it is `fun _ -> ApplicableAttribute`, and change its `extract` to yield `transparencyOf constant` for a constant material and `DiscreteValue (transparencyKey Absorbing)` for every dispersive material (classified via `materialDispersion` `MaterialLibrary.fs:606-609`), so every dispersive material lands under Absorbing. Leave the multi-valued Dispersion-model, Film-material, and Film-thickness facets unchanged. Update `OpticalConstructor.Tests` (`LibraryFacetsTests`) to prove, over `builtInEntries`, that the Category, Anisotropy, Dispersion, and Transparency branch counts each sum to the material count and that every dispersive material appears under Absorbing.","acceptance":"After the gates are dropped, over the seed corpus the Category, Anisotropy, Dispersion, and Transparency facet branch counts MUST each sum to the material count and every dispersive material MUST appear under Absorbing - unit-verified."}
{"number":6,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Restrict the gyration and mu preview charts to the applicable components (operator, Part C). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`: change `gyrationChart` (`:110-130`) to take the entry's gyration class and emit ONE series per component that `gyrationComponents` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:436-444`) admits for that class, naming each with `gyrationComponentLabel` (`:421-428`) and reading `Im[rho.[i,j]]` at the (i,j) slot each `GyrationComponent` denotes (`:88-94`); change `muChart` (`:141-162`) to take the entry's `MuKind` (`:72-74`) and emit a single scalar mu component for `ScalarMuKind` versus the diagonal-plus-gyration set for `GyromagneticMuKind`. Thread the class/kind at the call sites (`MaterialEditorView.fs:1028-1046`): from `m.editor.gyration` and the editor's magnetic `MuKind` for an `EditableMaterial`, and for a `ViewOnlyMaterial` from the stored `complexity` value tree - mirroring `anisotropyOfEntry` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:74-77`); a coded preset with no stored tree keeps the current all-components rendering. Update `NkDispersionChartTests` and `MaterialEditorWindowTests` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`.","acceptance":"After the change, a uniaxial-active entry's gyration chart MUST carry only g11 and g33 with matching names, a scalar-mu entry's mu chart MUST carry only its single mu component, and a coded preset with no stored tree MUST still render all components - headless-verified.","section":"Part C - Material-editor charts"}
{"number":7,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Make the material-editor description `TextBox` wrap instead of clip (minor, Part C.2). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs` set the description box to `AcceptsReturn true` and `TextWrapping = TextWrapping.Wrap` and give it a `MinWidth` inside the left pane so it grows multiline rather than meeting the splitter and clipping. No other layout change. Add a headless assertion in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` that the description box carries wrapping enabled.","acceptance":"After the change, the material-editor description box MUST wrap to multiple lines rather than clip when narrowed - headless-verified that wrapping is enabled."}
{"number":8,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Require a substrate on a Plate (operator, Part D.1). Extend `validateSample` (`ElementId.fs:802-811`) so that, in addition to the existing blank-name and structurally-empty checks, a sample whose `substrate` is `Plate` (`SubstrateKind`, `:80-82`) but whose `structure.substrate` (`:135-144`) is `None` returns `Error (InvalidSample <reason>)`. A `ThinFilm` sample is unaffected. Add `OpticalConstructor.Tests` cases: a `Plate` with `structure.substrate = None` is `InvalidSample`; the same `Plate` with `Some` substrate and a non-blank name is `Ok`; a `ThinFilm` with no substrate stays `Ok`.","acceptance":"After the extension, `validateSample` MUST reject a `Plate` whose `structure.substrate` is `None` with a typed `InvalidSample`, while a `ThinFilm` with no substrate stays `Ok` - unit-verified.","section":"Part D - Sample geometry and R/T"}
{"number":9,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[8],"how_to":"Give `Sample` a geometry-constrained supported-emission (operator 010/Q3, Part D.2). Add `supportedEmission : Emission` to the `Sample` record (`ElementId.fs:178-188`) reusing the existing DU (`Placement.fs:108-138`). Enforce the invariant that a `ThinFilm` sample's `supportedEmission` is always `EmitReflectedOnly` and a `Plate` defaults to `EmitBoth` - express it as one pure helper (e.g. `defaultSupportedEmission : SubstrateKind -> Emission` plus a `constrainEmission : SubstrateKind -> Emission -> Emission` that forces `EmitReflectedOnly` under `ThinFilm`), so a thin film can never clear its R branch. Set the field on every seeded sample (all `ThinFilm`, so `EmitReflectedOnly`) at `ElementId.fs:539` and the sibling seeds (`:557`,`:583`,`:608`,`:617`,`:626`,`:649`). Update every `Sample` constructor and consumer mechanically to compile. Unit tests in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` cover the ThinFilm-forced invariant, the Plate default, and that clearing a Plate's R via `Emission.withReflected false` leaves T on.","acceptance":"After the field is added, a `ThinFilm` sample's `supportedEmission` MUST be `EmitReflectedOnly` and unclearable, a `Plate` MUST default to `EmitBoth` and be constrainable to R-only or T-only through the existing setters, and every seed builds - unit-verified."}
{"number":10,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[9],"how_to":"Expose sample R/T in the editor (Part D.2). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorView.fs` add `supportedEmission` to the editor `Model` (`:120-146`), initialise it in `init` (`:333-366`) from the edited sample (or `defaultSupportedEmission` of the geometry for a new sample), carry it into `toSample` (`:369-376`), and include it in the dirty snapshot `SampleEditSnapshot` (`:110`) and `currentEdit` (`:314-315`) so an emission change marks the editor dirty. Render R and T checkboxes driven by `Emission.withReflected` / `withTransmitted` (`Placement.fs:126-138`) with a `Msg` + `update` arm, shown only for a `Plate`; a `ThinFilm` shows R fixed-on and disabled (the invariant from step 9). Give the checkboxes stable `UiIds.SampleEditor` AutomationIds. Headless tests in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`: a Plate editor toggles T off leaving R on and marks dirty; clearing both is impossible; a ThinFilm editor shows R fixed and no T control.","acceptance":"After the change, a Plate sample editor MUST let the user constrain emission to R-only or T-only via the checkboxes (never neither, marking the editor dirty) while a ThinFilm editor MUST show R fixed on - headless-verified."}
{"number":11,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[10],"how_to":"Let a film-less Plate set its substrate through the Materials Select window (operator, Part D.4). Add a `SampleSubstrateTarget` case to `SelectionTarget` (`WindowMode.fs:31-33`) beside `SampleLayerTarget`. In `SampleEditorView.fs` give the substrate Set... its own material-pick verb modelled on `chooseMaterialForLayer` (`:700-720`) that opens the Materials window in Select state with `target = SampleSubstrateTarget`, replacing the `hasChosenMaterial`-gated 'Set from chosen' substrate button (`:961`, `:921-922`) as the substrate path; route the targeted `onSelected` return to `SampleStackMsg.SetSubstrate (Some <layer>)` (`SampleStackEditor.fs:95`,`:367`), a vanished editor being a no-op plus status line. Handle the new target case where the Materials window resolves its Select target and its target description (`MaterialsWindowView.fs`, e.g. `:857`). Headless tests in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`: a Plate with no films opens the Materials Select window from the substrate Set... verb and the returned material becomes its substrate.","acceptance":"After the change, a film-less Plate MUST be able to set its substrate by picking a material through the Materials window in Select state targeted at the substrate slot - headless-verified."}
{"number":12,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D5","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[9],"how_to":"Bound the placed element and the experiment by the sample's supported emission (Part D.3). When a sample is placed on the table, derive its default `Placement.emission` from the bound sample's `supportedEmission` rather than the generic `defaultEmission` (`Placement.fs:168-171`) - locate the sample-placement path (the palette/add-to-table flow that builds a `Placement` for a sample element) and seed its emission from the bound sample. Default the experiment's `MeasurementMode` for a varied sample from the same value through the existing `MeasurementMode.ofEmission` (`Experiments.fs:106-110`); when the sample supports both, the experiment MAY still capture R, T, or both. Add coverage: a placed `ThinFilm` sample defaults to `EmitReflectedOnly` and its experiment to `CaptureReflected`; a `Plate` supporting both defaults to `EmitBoth` / `CaptureBoth` - unit tests in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` plus a headless assertion in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`.","acceptance":"After the change, a placed sample's default emission and its experiment's default `MeasurementMode` MUST both derive from the sample's `supportedEmission` (a ThinFilm sample defaulting to reflected-only) - unit- and headless-verified."}
{"number":13,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-W1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,5,6,7,10,11,12],"how_to":"Finalise the composition: confirm every window that consumes the changed surfaces still composes at the App root (`OpticalConstructor.App`) and drive the whole surface headless. The `ui-smoke` suite in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` MUST render one frame each - without throwing - for the Materials window (collapsed sorted tree, visible selection), the Library window (same), the Material editor (restricted gyration/mu tabs, wrapping description), and the Sample editor (R/T checkboxes for a Plate, R fixed for a ThinFilm, substrate Set... via Materials Select). No new wiring is introduced beyond the steps above.","acceptance":"After composition, the `ui-smoke` suite MUST render the Materials and Library windows, the Material editor, and the Sample editor over the new tree/chart/emission behaviour without throwing, and every test gate MUST be at or above its baseline count."}
